if you're trying to get your YouTube  channel launched today's video talks  about the top five mistakes that new  youtubers make when launching their  channel and how to stop sucking on  camera so I got a question for one of my  YouTube viewers Patricia love you guys  who wrote in to say hey Evan I have a  problem with my videos actually several  problems welcome to the club but the one  that I'm concerned about the most is  that I think they're too dull boring and  repetitive I want to get people's  attention but I can't do it by saying  the same thing again and again what  would you recommend to shake up a little  bit more about my videos thanks for this  video it helped a lot this is a  fantastic question and I think every  youtuber struggles on their journey to  eventually achieving success and I've  definitely learned a lot on my journey  from starting with nothing to having  millions of views on my channel I'm  going to share with you the five  mistakes that most newbie youtubers make  and how you can avoid sucking on camera  so number one is having no passion so  many new youtubers have zero passion and  emotion in their videos and I get why  you do it you know you're nervous in  front of the camera here you're not used  to speaking to a screen you don't have  an audience in front of you that you can  get energy from you also might be trying  to remember the script and say exactly  the words that you want to say and get  exactly the message out that you want to  get out and the end result is a super  boring video I remember one of my first  videos let's link it up here was on Walt  Disney and I had a professional video  crew come in and I had a script that I  memorized that I wanted to be perfect  and and it looked great the setup was  perfect but because I was so nervous  because I was just speaking to a camera  because I wanted to get the exact words  out my delivery sucked and I would use  passionate words with no passion I would  say things like to learn from Walt  Disney you need to make sure that you  follow your passion so boring right so  you've got to tap into your passion  you've got to stop boring about scene  exact words exactly as you wrote them  down and instead let the emotion come  through and have more passion every  video that you create how you say  something is equally as important as  what you're saying  so inject more passion into your videos  number two is repeating yourself if you  watch a lot of newbie youtubers in their  videos are saying the same thing over  and over and over again and and maybe  finding three different ways to say the  exact same message you need to practice  getting your message to be concise one  exercise that really helped me that my  media coach gave me is to practice doing  one-minute Mondays where basically I had  to deliver a message and a story and  something impactful in under two minutes  and do that every single week on my  channel and at first it was really hard  I couldn't get anything out in under two  minutes and I thought I have so much to  say I have so many stories I want to get  it out there but when I look back on my  old videos I realized I just kept saying  the same thing over and over and over  again and using different words so  practice your own version of a  one-minute Monday so you can get concise  thinking and execution of your ideas  number three is summarizing and not  being specific a lot of newbie youtubers  are not great storytellers they're  telling their story they're explaining  something that was traumatic in their  life or life-changing that happened  before and you just give the high level  summary instead of making me feel like  I'm a part of the story this is  something I had a huge problem with  myself as I was trying to develop my  channel and get better as a speaker I  would talk about a major problem I had  and say and that was a really tough  period in my life and so I decided I  really had to turn things around I would  give very few details and wasn't very  specific at all where instead it's  better to talk about fewer points but go  deeper on them if you're talking about a  time in your life where you are really  struggling take me there  make it feel like I'm sitting next to  you on the couch watching it happen tell  me about how you were crying and how the  the tears were coming out of your eyes  and your nose and tell me about how your  mother came and put her hand on your  shoulder and told you that everything  was going to be okay tell me what you  were thinking feeling acting tell me  about it  make me again feel like I am right  they're watching with you instead of  being up here where I'm disconnected and  I don't really understand what's going  on  so stop summarizing and start being  specific number four is not  personalizing your videos wherever  possible you want to be able to tell a  personal story to help bring your point  home your story not only helps people  connect to you more but also helps drive  your point home so in my first point I  was talking about not having passion I  shared an example but my first Disney  video that you can go back and click on  in my second point about repeating  yourself I shared an example about how I  kept repeating myself and used a  one-minute Monday exercise that helped  me get through so try to add a personal  story or anecdote to every single video  that you make you'll often find that the  best stories are the ones that make you  vulnerable where you're talking about  real problems that you have I've made  videos talking about my divorce my hair  loss my weight gain as struggles that I  faced when I was growing my business I  talked about how I was making $300 a  month barely able to survive feeling  totally worthless feeling totally  helpless feeling like I added no value  to the world and I didn't know what to  do with my life  and that can be really hard to do  because in general you want to present a  positive picture when you go out and you  meet people and they ask you how you are  that the default answer is I'm fine  we're really maybe you're not so fine  and if you look at the top youtubers  they're willing to share their  vulnerabilities they're willing to share  their stories and they're willing to be  naked figuratively in front of the  camera so start sharing and start  getting more personalized number 5 is  your videos are important enough my  agent liked to tell me when we first  started working together that my videos  they weren't important enough he always  used to say I had to up the stakes every  time I got off a call with him when he  reviewed my videos he said up the stakes  up the ante make it more important and  it's true if your videos are more  important if you go in with the  intention of the videos being important  then that makes a quality that much  better here  exercise that I like to do before I get  on camera I imagine someone who's having  a problem who's going through something  really important in their life and who  needs help  I imagine that my video is the last  thing that they're going to watch before  they make this all-important decision if  a video is talking about self-confidence  for example I might imagine somebody  who's just about to jump off a bridge  and kill themselves and my video is the  last thing that they are going to watch  before they make that super important  life decision that makes me feel like  the video that I'm about to create is  more important and when I feel like it's  more important than I'm going to project  that importance on to you now the  reality is it's not going to be that  important for most people but it will be  that important for some people and  unless you project yourself with the  confidence and with that important stake  in mind you're not going to hit those  people I do videos helping entrepreneurs  but I've had people who wrote to me  saying Evan your videos have saved my  life that's important and so you need to  approach your videos with that same  level of importance the next time you  step in front of the camera you want to  be thinking the video that I'm making  right now has the ability to change or  save somebody's life make your videos  more important start to up the ante and  people will start to care a lot more and  my sixth bonus tip is actually care I  think it's by default for most youtubers  that you care about your audience you  care about what you're doing I feel the  love from patricia's , that she's  genuinely trying to make videos that  people will care about some youtubers  don't care they're just trying to put  videos up there to try to make a lot of  money they're trying to monetize who  advertise in ourselves some affiliate  programs if you don't actually care  about your audience then there's no way  that they're actually going to care  about you so those are my five plus one  tips on the mistakes that most beginners  make on how to stop sucking on camera  and of course remember to continue to  believe for those are you watching if  you like this video you want to see more  don't forget to subscribe to the channel  thank you so much for tuning in and I'll  see you soon  South improvement books are like Fitness  books they never work on their own what  you need is a trainer that's ever get  the newsletter  you

